Position: Senior React Native / React Engineer
Format: remote, full-time
Contacts: @lilz_e · zelenskii19992017@gmail.com
LinkedIn: linkedin.com/in/lilzee
Salary expectations: $45/hr

About me

I've been building mobile and web apps with React Native, React and TypeScript for more than six years. For five years I've worked at Batch, a US group-travel service. For the last two years I've run the mobile app on my own and done a lot of the web side: I started the partner portal from scratch.

Experience at Batch

Mobile:
• search and booking: filters, real-time availability, Stripe payments;
• maps: places in a city, the trip plan, locations on place pages;
• social features: event calendar with RSVPs, polls, shared expenses, chat;
• a TikTok-style vertical video feed, moved from react-native-video to expo-video;
• push notifications, analytics, A/B tests, OTA updates, monitoring;
• three rebrands and major redesigns of the app;
• moved all heavy lists to FlashList;
• moved to the New Architecture and enabled R8: the Android build got 29% smaller (124 → 88 MB);
• a big performance overhaul: profiling showed that NativeWind interop wrappers and lucide SVG icons put the most load on the JS thread in large lists. I removed them from heavy rows, which roughly halved rendering work, ended long freezes and sped up cold start. The trip screen now opens almost instantly (0.15 s instead of 3.6 s), picking a date in the booking calendar takes about 0.25 s instead of 1.5 s, map pins appear noticeably faster, and the place page and trip-plan map run smoother;
• a native Expo module in Swift and Kotlin for the HubSpot Mobile Chat SDK, to move support chat from Intercom to HubSpot.

Web:
• partner portal on TanStack Start: partner onboarding, plans and subscriptions on Stripe, leads, media library, user-generated content collection, promo pages for paid modules, analytics;
• Next.js marketplace: place, partner and trip pages, map search on Google Maps, request-a-quote form, booking;
• Turborepo monorepo: the mobile app, the marketplace and the portal on shared packages.

Cost savings:
• proposed and removed the Google Places API, which took a noticeable share of the budget;
• image and video optimisation through ImageKit in the mobile app and on the web, so right-sized files load instead of originals;
• moving support chat from Intercom to HubSpot.

Other projects

• ARI Athletics — an app for coaches who recruit athletes;
• Premium Chat — a messenger: a React Native app and a real-time WebSocket layer, both written from scratch.

Stack

• Mobile: React Native (New Architecture), Expo, Expo Modules (Swift, Kotlin), TypeScript, Reanimated, Gesture Handler, FlashList, React Navigation, NativeWind, expo-video, react-native-maps, React Compiler
• Web: React, Next.js (App Router, RSC), TanStack Start / Router / Query / Table / Virtual, Tailwind, Radix UI, XState, Vite, Astro, Google Maps
• Data & forms: Redux Toolkit, RTK Query, react-hook-form, zod
• Infrastructure: Turborepo, pnpm, GitHub Actions, Vercel, EAS, fastlane, OTA updates, AWS (Amplify, Cognito, S3)
• Monitoring: Sentry, Crashlytics, Firebase Performance
• Analytics & experiments: Firebase, Mixpanel, AppsFlyer, GrowthBook, Microsoft Clarity
• Integrations: Stripe, Iterable, Intercom, HubSpot, GetStream, ImageKit, push notifications (FCM / APNs), deep links
• Testing & code quality: Jest, Vitest, Testing Library, oxlint, husky

Looking for

A mobile or frontend role in a product team, remote. I'm also open to fullstack roles on React Native and Next.js.

If you have a matching role, message me: @lilz_e.
